\f0\b \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Components of Selenium webdriver
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Webdriver Bindings:
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 \'a0Selenium provides a set of commands which can be written using different languages.\'a0 Since Selenium Supports many languages like Java, C#, Python, etc. each language has a set of selenium commands design, as per programming languages standards. Selenium always ensures that similar commands are available for all the supported languages to perform an interaction with the browser. Using the command one can write the selenium test automation scripts.\

\f0\b \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Driver:
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 \'a0Drivers are browser-specific for example If we want to run our scripts on Chrome Browser, we need to have ChromeDriver in place, likewise for Firefox and Edge. The Driver helps to control the browser behavior.\

\f0\b \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Browsers:
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 \'a0Browsers are the actual browsers like Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari, etc, the commands will be executed, and the interactions can be seen visually.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec3 5.\'a0What is the advantage of Selenium.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Advantages of Selenium
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf4 \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Open Source:
\f1\b0 \'a0Selenium is shipped with Apache 2.0 License which means that it is open-source anyone can use. No need to purchase.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Cross Browser Support:
\f1\b0 \'a0Selenium Supports almost all major browsers Firefox, Chrome, IE, Edge, Firefox, Safari. So, all our use cases related to cross-browser testing can be covered using Selenium.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Cross-Platform Support:
\f1\b0 \'a0Selenium can be used and run tests across multiple platforms such as Windows, Linux, and Mac-based machines.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Well Written Documentation:
\f1\b0 \'a0Selenium has documented everything, which is easy for anyone to refer to and implement the same. Selenium has recently updated documentation where we can search for any commands APIs provided by selenium it describes the same.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Community Support:
\f1\b0 \'a0Since Selenium is used by thousands of uses, community support is good, most of the questions are already answered on various forums. Apart from that, there are tons of tutorial which makes our job easier.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Language Support:
\f1\b0 \'a0Selenium Support many languages JavaScript (Node.js), Python, Ruby, Java, and C#, etc. Bindings are updated more often to ensure all the features are available across the selenium-supported languages.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 High Customization:
\f1\b0 \'a0There are many modern web automation frameworks that come as Framework Ready, most of the framework restricts customization, or customization is limited to some extent. The Selenium shipped in pure format, you can customize the way you want. Many organizations created frameworks combining selenium and many other tools.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Simulate almost everything:
\f1\b0 \'a0Whether it is a keyboard event, mouse event Selenium doesn\'92t restrict this, almost all the events can be simulated to interact with the browser.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Support for Chrome DevTools:
\f1\b0 \'a0The latest Selenium 4 has also introduced the feature called Chrome DevTools Support, This is the major feature of Selenium 4 with this feature one can Emulate the Network Bandwidth, Block Urls, Mock API calls, Emulate Devices, Emulate Geo Location many more.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Screenshot Support:
\f1\b0 \'a0The Selenium Screenshot support is introduced in Selenium 4, Screenshot can be taken at the page level or Web Element Level with just a few lines of code.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Selector Support:
\f1\b0 \'a0Selenium allows to use of different types of selectors like XPath, CSS, ID, Class, etc. we are not restricted here.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

