\f0\b\fs48 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 27.\'a0How to handle hidden element in Selenium?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs36 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 A hidden element means that Element is present in DOM but it is not visible in the browser. To handle the hidden element in Selenium, we need to use the JavaScript Executor.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 For Example:\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Consider we have a hidden text box with id="hiddenbox1".\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 JavascriptExecutor executor = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 String str = (String) executor.executeScript("return document.getElementById('hiddenbox1').value");\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Though, the hiddenbox1 is not visible on the browser, since the text box is attached to DOM we can get the value of the text box using the above method.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

