\f0\b\fs48 \cf4 \cb2 29.\'a0How to read data from excel in selenium webdriver?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs36 \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Selenium Webdriver doesn\'92t provide any functionality to work with an excel file. However, reading and writing data into excel can be done using Java Utility called POI\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Apache POI is an open-source java library used to handle Microsoft Office-based files. This helps the user to perform the operation on excel files such as read, write, etc.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Once you add the Apache POI jar to your project you can use the library utilities to read/write data into Excel File.\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Example:
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 FileInputStream fs = new FileInputStream("D:\\\\Example.xlsx");\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 XSSFWorkbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(fs);\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 XSSFSheet sheet = workbook.getSheetAt(0);\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Row row = sheet.getRow(0);\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Cell cell = row.getCell(0);\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 System.out.println(sheet.getRow(0).getCell(0));\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
